When rebuilding an existing endpoint, I get a few things first:

Note that if the boss VM is not running, start it.

Log into the control node and copy the rfmonitor config
to Mothership boss and put it in ~stoller/powder/systems/XXX

	control> scp /etc/rfmonitor/device_config.json boss.emulab.net:

On the boss, grab interfaces info and copy to Mothership boss and put
it in ~stoller/powder/systems/XXX

	boss> echo 'select node_id,iface,role,ip,mac from interfaces;' | mysql -t tbdb > /tmp/iface.txt
	boss> scp /tmp/iface.txt boss.emulab.net: 

Grab a copy of the DB and copy to Mothership boss and put it in
~stoller/powder/systems/XXX

	boss> mysqldump --skip-opt tbdb | gzip > /tmp/tbdb.sql.gz
	boss> scp /tmp/tbdb.sql.gz boss.emulab.net:

Now use the interfaces info to update the files in ~stoller/powder/systems/XXX
If the node.txt is space delimited, needs to be fixed up. Look at one of the
other buses.

Before removing the old disk from the endpoint

        msboss> manage_aggregate EBC chflag admin yes

Before starting the elabinelab:

	msboss> sudo /usr/testbed/sbin/protogeni/cacontrol -R -r boss.<aggregate>.powderwireless.net

And update the ns file for experiment elab-febuild (or elab-mebuild2).
You need to change:

	CONFIG_NICKNAME (.defs files POWDER_NICKNAME value)
	TARGETSYS_DOMAIN
	TARGETSYS_NETWORK
	TARGETSYS_ROUTER
	TARGETSYS_BOSSIP
	TARGETSYS_HOMEBASE (where does this come from?)
	SSLCERT_ORGNAME
	XEN_STARTUPSCRIPT (rc.powder argument first arg should be router IP)


------

Fire up the elabinelab.

Once the VMs are ready, copy the directory mentioned above over to the
inner boss as /usr/testbed/etc/targetsys. Do NOT put this stuff on the
inner ops!

	msboss> sudo scp -rp ~stoller/powder/systems/XXX
	         	pcvmXXX-1:/usr/testbed/etc/targetsys

Sync the apt package mirror. You need the msboss elabman ssh key in your agent. 

	msboss> ~/testbed/testbed/install/powder-fixed/syncmirror.sh pcvmXXX-1

Now we convert the VMs for boot in the target environment:

First ssh (as root) into inner ops:

	ops> cd /usr/testbed/obj/testbed/install
	ops> perl emulab-install -b -i ops/targetsys ops
	ops> perl emulab-install -b -i ops/powder-endpoint ops

Now ssh (as root) into the inner boss VM from outer boss:

	boss> cd /usr/testbed/obj/testbed/install
	boss> perl emulab-install -b -i boss/targetsys boss
	boss> cd /users/elabman/emulab-devel/obj/install
	boss> perl emulab-install -b -i boss/powder-endpoint boss
	boss> exit

Add these to both inner boss/ops /etc/mail/aliases and run newaliases:
	
	# Send everything to the Mothership.
	testbed-ops:            powder-aggregate-ops@emulab.net
	testbed-logs:           powder-aggregate-logs@emulab.net
	testbed-www:            powder-aggregate-www@emulab.net
	testbed-approval:       powder-aggregate-approval@emulab.net
	testbed-audit:          powder-aggregate-audit@emulab.net
	testbed-stated:         powder-aggregate-stated@emulab.net
	testbed-testsuite:      powder-aggregate-testsuite@emulab.net
	testbed-errors:         powder-aggregate-errors@emulab.net
	testbed-automail:       powder-aggregate-automail@emulab.net

Grab (inner) boss:/usr/testbed/etc/elabman.pswd and save it:

     	msboss:~stoller/powder/systems/xxx/elabman.pswd

Fix for ntpdate:
        boss> echo '155.98.33.74    ntp1.emulab.net ntp1' | sudo bash -c '/bin/cat >> /etc/hosts'

Copy MFS tar ball to boss while the network is good:

	msboss> sudo scp ~mike/FE.tar.gz XXX:/tftpboot

Now we have to shutdown the VMs. Log out of the boss/ops vms, and log
into the physical host and then:

	vhost-0> sudo /usr/local/etc/emulab/vnodesetup -jh pcvmXXX-1

Make sure its really gone, then toss the token to David.

While waiting for the token, approve the certificate on the MotherShip.

	msboss> sudo /usr/testbed/sbin/protogeni/cacontrol -c boss.<aggregate>.powderwireless.net
	msboss> sudo /usr/local/etc/rc.d/2.portalpsd.sh stop
	msboss> sudo /usr/local/etc/rc.d/2.portalpsd.sh start

If a brand new install, add the named entries to bas and ddc named server.
	
	bas> sudo /usr/local/etc/rc.d/named restart
	ns5> sudo /usr/local/etc/rc.d/named restart

Wait wait wait, for the token from David.
After David does his magic and boss boots then:

Log into the new control node and remove the symlink in /etc/xen/auto,
We wil put ths back once the enpoint is installed and things are working
okay. Saves on filesystem corruptions.

	control> sudo rm /etc/xen/auto/boss.conf

But start the VM if it is not running. When building an ME, it will
not be running:

	control> sudo xl create /etc/xen/boss.conf

Then login to boss.

Add the special interface that allows monitoring to work:

    	# ME
	boss> wap addinterface -t P2PLTE -e expt ed1 rf0
	OR
	# FE
	boss> wap addinterface -t P2PLTE -e expt nuc2 rf0

And some other tidbits that should be automated:

	boss> wap update_sitevars 
	boss> wap addservers
        boss> sudo getcacerts -f
	boss> sudo /bin/rm -rf `cat /users/elabman/emulab-devel/emulab-devel/install/powder-fixed/rmfiles.txt`
	boss> sudo mv /etc/emulab /etc/emulab.old
	boss> sudo mv /usr/local/etc/emulab /usr/local/etc/emulab.old
	boss> sudo testbed-control boot

Unpack the MFSs:

	boss> cd /tftpboot
	boss> sudo tar xzf FE.tar.gz
	boss> cd NEW
	boss> sudo sh install.sh

Apply the boss/ops SSL patch:
        boss> scp boss.emulab.net:~mike/ssl-fix.tar.gz /tmp/
	boss> tar -C /tmp -xzf /tmp/ssl-fix.tar.gz
	boss> cd /tmp/ssl-fix; sudo sh fixssl.sh
	boss> sudo rm -rf /tmp/ssl-fix*

Re-install syncthing.
        Follow the instructions in powder/syncthing/README in the source tree.

Copy the defs file back to the MotherShip.

	boss> cd ~elabman/emulab-devel
	boss> cp defs-targetsys emulab-devel/powder-defs/XXX    (bus-5175)
	boss> scp defs-targetsys stoller@boss.emulab.net:testbed-noelvin/testbed/powder-defs/XXX
	boss> sudo rm defs-targetsys
	boss> ln -s emulab-devel/powder-defs/XXX defs-targetsys

Be sure to commit the new defs file.

Do the letsencrypt dance:

	boss> cd ~elabman/emulab-devel/obj/install
	boss> sudo perl emulab-install -b -i letsencrypt boss

Shutdown the boss VM and wait until it is installed.

-----

After installation in the endpoint:

Copy over Jie's monitor:

	msboss> cd ~stoller/testbed-noelvin
	msboss> rsync -av -C rfmonitor-jie elabman@control.<aggregate>.powderwireless.net:

Install Jie's monitor:

	control> cd ~elabman/rfmonitor-jie
	control> sudo systemctl stop rfmonitor
	control> sudo python3 setup.py install
	control> (cd /usr/bin; sudo rm -f rfmonitor; sudo ln -s /usr/local/bin/rfmonitor .)

Setup the rfmonitor config file. Either copy it from the old disk, or
create a new one by creating /etc/rfmonitor/device_config.json:

  Bus:
	{
	    "devices" : {
	      "ed1:rf0"  : {
	        "name" : "ed1:rf0",
	        "channels" : {"0" : "TX/RX", "1" : "TX/RX"},
	        "direction" : {"incident" : "0", "transmit" : "1"}
	      }
	    }
	}

   Endpoint:
	{
	    "devices" : {
	      "nuc2:rf0"  : {
	        "name" : "nuc2:rf0",
	        "channels" : {"0" : "TX/RX", "1" : "TX/RX"},
	        "direction" : {"incident" : "0", "transmit" : "1"}
	      }
	    }
	}

    About direction: Flip a coin. Heads, set incident to 0 and transmit to 1.
    Tails, set incident to 1 and transmit to 0.

Run the noise calibration. I have no idea what this does:

	control> cd ~elabman/rfmonitor-jie
	control> (cd scripts; sudo ./run_noisefloor_calibration.sh)

Start the monitor. Hopefully you see it in ps and it is not in a death loop.

	control> sudo systemctl start rfmonitor

Start up the boss VM:

	control> sudo xl create /etc/xen/boss.conf

Make sure the monitor reports are coming in every couple of minutes:

	boss> tail -f /usr/testbed/log/rfmonitor_daemon.log

Enable the deadman radio watcher:

       boss> wap setsitevar powder/deadman_enable 1

Make sure the arduino is doing the right thing:

	boss> tail -f /usr/testbed/log/endpoint-monitor.log

    On an FE:
	Oct 28 13:42:33 : keepalive: 1761680553
	Oct 28 13:42:33 : New tempF: 66.650
	Oct 28 13:42:33 : temp:66.5564
	Oct 28 13:42:47 : keepalive: 1761680567
	Oct 28 13:42:47 : New tempF: 66.650
	Oct 28 13:42:47 : temp:66.5834

    On an ME:
	Oct 28 13:45:11 : New tempF: 89.492
	Oct 28 13:45:11 : temp:89.4164, onbat:0, voltage:12.084, current:7.380, v':12.409
	Oct 28 13:45:25 : keepalive: 1761680725
	Oct 28 13:45:25 : New tempF: 89.492
	Oct 28 13:45:25 : temp:89.429, onbat:0, voltage:12.182, current:5.327, v':12.416

Free the nodes from hwdown:

	boss> wap nfree emulab-ops hwdown ed1 (or nuc1 nuc2)

Now for the fun part! Start this experiment in the emulab-ops project:
Be sure to select correct radio or FE or ME. Delete the spectrum range!

	https://www.powderwireless.net/show-profile.php?profile=6328aa9e-7c99-11e9-8a5c-e4434b2381fc

On boss start this up:

	tail -f /usr/testbed/log/rfmonitor_daemon.log

And log into the experiment node and run:

	node> /usr/libexec/uhd/examples/tx_waveforms --ant TX/RX --channel 0 --rate 1e6 --freq 3550e6 --gain 50

    Let it run while watching the output from rfmonitor_daemon.log. It might take
    till the second report to see anything. Ideally you want to see this:

    	Above floor:-110.0 ed1:rf0: 3550,-104.455875279867,3556.0
	No interface limit info for ed1
	New previous data:
	$VAR1 = {
		  'ed1:rf0:3550' => {
                              'node_id' => 'ed1',
                              'frequency' => '3550.0',
                              'instance' => undef,
                              'incident' => undef,
                              'power' => '-104.45587527986746',
                              'center' => '3556.0',
                              'violation' => 0,
                              'iface' => 'rf0',
                              'repeatcount' => 0,
                              'abovefloor' => '5.54412472013254',
                              'timestamp' => 1761689300
                            }
		};

    If after another iteration or two there is nothing or if you see stuff on totally
    other frequenceies, you can stop. You probably had a bad coin flip up above. Reverse
    incident and transmit and rerun the noise calculation, restart the rfmonitor (all this
    on the control node. Then rerun the transmit test. Hopefully you see something then

Restore symlink in /etc/xen/auto

	control> cd /etc/xen/auto
	control> sudo ln -s ../boss.conf .

Let the bus roam:

	msboss> manage_aggregate Bus6365 chflag admin no

QED
